1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:02,610
 So what is Android? As many of you probably already

2
00:00:02,610 --> 00:00:06,790
 know, Android is an operating system designed for mobile devices. Where

3
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:09,760
 mobile devices are devices that are, of course, mobile, and

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:12,750
 that are characterized by the fact of having touch screens and

5
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:15,930
 sensors. Typical examples would be smart phones, like the one

6
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:18,400
 that you probably have in your pocket, and tablets, that are

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,260
 very commonly used nowadays. An

8
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:22,110
 important characteristic of the Android operating

9
00:00:22,110 --> 00:00:25,400
 system, it is based on the Linux kernel. So it is

10
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,760
 running customized version of the Linux kernel. And in order

11
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:31,196
 to be able to run application, it is powered by

12
00:00:31,196 --> 00:00:35,130
 a Java-based virtual machine, which is called the Dalvik VM.

13
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:37,750
 The Dalvik VM is a type of JVM which is used

14
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:40,950
 in Android devices to run applications. An important point about

15
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:43,830
 the Dalvik VM is that it is optimized for mobile

16
00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:46,480
 devices. What that means is that it is optimized for

17
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:47,790
 low processing power and low

18
00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:51,170
 memory environments. Therefore, Android applications or

19
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:53,010
 Android apps, as we normally call them,

20
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:53,010
 are Java-based applications that run on Dalvik.

